 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with a pause that grows by 2 seconds after each
+one: 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds, `ATTEMPTS` and `BACKOFF_SECONDS` in `larder/capture.py`. When the fifth attempt times
+out, the capture fails with `GatewayTimeout`.
+
+Captures used to make 3 attempts, back to back, all within one second. The gateway answers slowly every Friday from
+17:00 to 19:00, its peak, so all three attempts landed in the same slow minute. One Friday, 58 confirmed pantry orders
+were never charged, and a payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's dashboard the next morning.
+Switching gateways was ruled out because the contract runs to December 2026. Replaying that Friday's timeouts against
+the gateway's sandbox showed that 5 attempts with these pauses would have captured 57 of the 58.
 
 Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
 can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
 drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
 
+## Known limits
+
+- The capture runs while the member waits on the confirmation page, so the pauses can keep them waiting up to 20
+  seconds longer. The maintainers decided this was better than volunteers capturing orders by hand.
+- A pantry order whose fifth attempt times out stays uncharged. Workaround: capture it by hand from the gateway's
+  dashboard, after [Gateway timeouts](../runbooks/gateway-timeouts.md) finds it in the worker's log.
+
